      "output": "```js\nconst LEVEL = [\n  \"..........................................................................................\",\n  \"..........................................................................................\",\n  \"..........................................................................................\",\n  \".............................................................................L............\",\n  \"............................................................................AAAA..........\",\n  \"..............................................................................T...........\",\n  \".......................................................................................M..\",\n  \".......................................................................###################\",\n  \"...............................................L.......................###################\",\n  \"..............AAA.....................................AAAA.........===.###################\",\n  \"...............T...............................^^......T....C..........###################\",\n  \".............................................######.........######.....###################\",\n  \"............######............C......=====....####..........######.....###################\",\n  \"..S.........######...#############..........................######.....###################\",\n  \"##################...#############..........................######.....###################\",\n  \"##################...#############..........................######.....###################\",\n  \"##################...#############..........................######.....###################\",\n];\n```\n\n- **Rooftop street (x0–33):** From S at (2,13), the fox steps up 2 to the roof at x12–17, then jumps up 3 to the awning at x14–16 for letter 1 at (15,8). It crosses a 3-tile gap at x18–20 to the street, where checkpoint 1 sits at (30,12).\n- **Floating stalls (x34–59):** A 3-tile gap leads up 1 to the plank at x37–41. Another 3-tile gap leads up 1 to the island at x45–50. On the island, the jump over the spikes at x47–48 collects letter 2 at (47,8): it is 2 tiles above the standing row, and peak height is about 3.75 tiles.\n- **Into stretch 3 (x58–70):** A 3-tile gap leads up 2 to the awning stall at x54–57. From there, a 2-tile gap drops 2 to the pillar at x60–65 with checkpoint 2 at (60,10). A 1-tile gap then leads up 2 to the plank at x67–69.\n- **Post office (x71–89):** A 1-tile gap leads up 2 to the post-office roof (top at row 7). From there, a 3-tile step up to the awning at x76–79 gives letter 3 at (77,3), and the mailbox is at (87,6). Across the whole map, no step is taller than 3 tiles and no gap is wider than 3 tiles.\n- **Unverified:** I counted the row lengths and the symbol totals (3 L, 2 C, 1 S, 1 M) by hand, and checked reachability only against the jump formulas. The map has not been playtested in a running build."
