      "outputType": "markdown",
      "output": "## Fox Courier: chiptune audio (Web Audio API, no audio files)\n\nPaste this snippet anywhere in the game's `<script>`. Loading it only declares constants and functions. It creates no AudioContext, starts no timer and reads no game objects.\n\n```js\n// Fox Courier chiptune: call sfx(name)/music(on) from game code; nothing runs at load.\nlet AC=null,master=null,musicGain=null,musicTimer=null,nextT=0,step=0;\nconst STEP=60/132/2, SC=[60,62,64,67,69,72,74,76,79,81], ROOT=[48,45,41,43,48,45,41,43];\nconst LEAD=[\"2345.43.\",\"4.5.643.\",\"5.4.5.67\",\"6...4.3.\",\"7.6.5.4.\",\"5.4.2.4.\",\"3.4.5.6.\",\"6.5.3.1.\"].join(\"\");\nconst mf=m=>440*Math.pow(2,(m-69)/12);\nconst SFX={\n  jump:[[\"square\",280,640,0,.13,.22]],\n  letter:[988,1319,1568,1976].map((f,i)=>[\"square\",f,f,i*.055,.09,.18]),\n  checkpoint:[523,659,784,1047].map((f,i)=>[\"triangle\",f,f,i*.08,.16,.35]).concat([[\"square\",1047,1047,.32,.25,.12]]),\n  win:[[523,0,.1],[659,.1,.1],[784,.2,.1],[1047,.3,.18],[784,.5,.1],[1047,.6,.6]].map(n=>[\"square\",n[0],n[0],n[1],n[2],.2]).concat([[\"triangle\",131,131,0,.3,.4],[\"triangle\",196,196,.3,.3,.4],[\"triangle\",262,262,.6,.6,.4]]),\n  fail:[[\"square\",440,110,0,.4,.2],[\"triangle\",220,55,0,.45,.35]],\n  restart:[[\"square\",880,220,0,.12,.15],[\"square\",330,660,.14,.12,.15]]};SFX.delivery=SFX.win;\nfunction audio(){\n  if(!AC){\n    const ua=navigator.userActivation, C=window.AudioContext||window.webkitAudioContext;\n    if(!C||(ua&&!ua.hasBeenActive))return null; // no user action yet: create nothing, stay silent\n    AC=new C(); master=AC.createGain(); master.gain.value=.3; master.connect(AC.destination);\n    musicGain=AC.createGain(); musicGain.gain.value=.6; musicGain.connect(master);\n  }\n  if(AC.state===\"suspended\")AC.resume(); return AC;\n}\nfunction tone(type,f0,f1,t,dur,vol,dest){\n  const o=AC.createOscillator(),g=AC.createGain(); o.type=type; o.frequency.setValueAtTime(f0,t);\n  if(f1!==f0)o.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(f1,t+dur);\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(.0001,t); g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(vol,t+.008); g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(.0001,t+dur);\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest||master); o.start(t); o.stop(t+dur+.02);\n}\nfunction sfx(name){\n  if(!audio()||!SFX[name])return;\n  const t=AC.currentTime+.01; SFX[name].forEach(n=>tone(n[0],n[1],n[2],t+n[3],n[4],n[5]));\n}\nfunction tick(){\n  while(nextT<AC.currentTime+.12){\n    const i=step%64,c=LEAD[i];\n    if(c!==\".\")tone(\"square\",mf(SC[+c]),mf(SC[+c]),nextT,STEP*.85,.14,musicGain);\n    if(i%2===0){const f=mf(ROOT[i>>3]+[0,12,7,12][(i>>1)%4]);tone(\"triangle\",f,f,nextT,STEP*1.8,.4,musicGain);}\n    nextT+=STEP; step++;\n  }\n}\nfunction music(on){\n  if(!on){if(musicTimer){clearInterval(musicTimer);musicTimer=null;}if(AC)musicGain.gain.setTargetAtTime(.0001,AC.currentTime,.03);return;}\n  if(!audio()||musicTimer)return;\n  musicGain.gain.cancelScheduledValues(AC.currentTime); musicGain.gain.setValueAtTime(.6,AC.currentTime); step=0; nextT=AC.currentTime+.06; tick(); musicTimer=setInterval(tick,25);\n}\n```\n\nThe snippet is 44 lines. All brackets are closed and there are no ellipses.\n\n### How the AudioContext stays behind the first user action\n- **Lazy creation:** `new AudioContext()` appears in only one place, inside `audio()`. `audio()` runs only when the game calls `sfx()` or `music()`.\n- **Activation check:** Where the browser exposes `navigator.userActivation`, `audio()` refuses to create the context until `hasBeenActive` is true. Until then, early calls are silent no-ops.\n- **Older browsers:** Where that API is missing, the guarantee depends on the game making its first `sfx()` or `music()` call from inside an input handler.\n- **Suspended context:** A suspended context is resumed on every call.\n\n### Hook-up for the game (from the Gameplay spec)\n| Game event | Call |\n|---|---|\n| Space/Enter on the title screen, which starts gameplay | `music(true)` inside the keydown handler |\n| Jump starts, after coyote/buffer logic | `sfx('jump')` |\n| Letter collected | `sfx('letter')` |\n| Checkpoint lantern lights, only when it advances | `sfx('checkpoint')` |\n| Mailbox touched with 3/3 letters | `music(false); sfx('win')` (`'delivery'` is an alias) |\n| Spike hit, or `y > 288` | `sfx('fail')` |\n| R pressed, or Space/R on the win screen | `sfx('restart'); music(true)` |\n\n### Sound design\n- **Jump:** A square-wave pitch sweep from 280 Hz up to 640 Hz.\n- **Letter pickup:** A fast four-note square arpeggio: B5, E6, G6, B6.\n- **Checkpoint:** A rising triangle arpeggio in C major, topped by a square-wave chime.\n- **Win/delivery:** A six-note square fanfare over a triangle bass.\n- **Fail:** A falling square and triangle \"drop\".\n- **Restart:** A short down-then-up blip.\n- **Music:** 132 BPM in eighth-note steps (about 0.227 s each), 8 bars × 8 steps, looping.\n  - The square lead uses the C-major pentatonic, with digits indexing into `SC` and `.` for a rest.\n  - The triangle bass plays the progression C–Am–F–G ×2 in quarter notes, using a root / octave / fifth / octave pattern.\n  - Notes are scheduled 120 ms ahead on a 25 ms interval. That interval is created only inside `music(true)`.\n\n### Unverified items\nThis snippet was **not executed in a browser**. I had no runtime here. The syntax, bracket balance and line count were checked by reading only, and no audio was heard. Still to verify:\n1. The snippet parses and plays in Chrome, Firefox and Safari. Safari uses the `webkitAudioContext` fallback.\n2. With `navigator.userActivation` present, no context is created before the first key press, and the first sound plays on that press.\n3. The mix levels (lead vs bass vs SFX), and whether the fail sweep sounds right.\n4. The loop has no gap or drift at the 64-step wrap.\n5. In background tabs, `setInterval` throttling may drop or bunch notes. Pausing music on `visibilitychange` may be needed.\n6. A quick `music(false)` → `music(true)` may let a few already-scheduled notes (up to 120 ms) overlap."
