      "output": "**Mode: static source review only. The build was not actually run.** No browser, input or audio test was performed. Every behaviour below is inferred from reading the source.\n\n**Confirmed in source**\n- **Keys:** ←/→ and A/D move. Space, ↑ and W jump. R calls `start()` from any state. Space or Enter restarts on the win screen.\n- **Tuning:** Values match the spec: gravity 0.32, max run speed 2, accel 0.25 / 0.15, jump −6.2, jump cut to −2, max fall 6.\n- **3-tile step:** The discrete jump rise is about 57 px, which clears the 48 px steps (tiles 12→14–16 and 71→76–79).\n- **Gaps:** The widest gap on the route is 3 tiles (18–20, 34–36, 42–44, 51–53).\n- **Tunnelling:** Speeds are at most 2 px horizontally and 6 px vertically, both below the 16 px tile size. Level edges count as solid.\n- **Camera:** Matches the spec formula, clamps to 0–960, and fixes Y at 1.\n- **Checkpoints:** Posts sit on solid ground at tiles 30 and 60. They only advance, and each shows a 60-frame toast.\n- **Death and respawn:** Death triggers on the spike bottom half or `y > 288`. The fade lasts 20 frames. Letters and the timer persist.\n- **Win:** Requires 3 letters. Otherwise the \"NEED 3 LETTERS!\" bubble appears. The timer freezes on delivery.\n- **External requests:** None. There are no URLs, fetch calls or fonts.\n\n**Defects found**\n1. **Map has only 2 letters.** The `LEVEL` map contains only two `L` tiles, and the third letter is patched in by code: `if(LT.length<3)LT.push({x:15,y:8})`. The HUD then lights `LT[i].g` in array order rather than collection order, so the first letter picked up lights the third icon.\n2. **No red-and-white awnings appear.** The awning choice uses `Math.floor(x/10)%2?IM.awnY:IM.awning`, and every awning sits at x = 14–16, 54–57 or 76–79. All three spans give an odd result, so every awning is yellow.\n3. **Best time is not saved.** `best` is held only in memory, and the source has no localStorage call.\n4. **Coyote time and jump buffer run about 5 frames instead of 6.** `f.jb--` runs before the `jb>0` check, and `co` counts down from 6.\n5. **Title screen differs from spec.** It shows \"PRESS ANY KEY\" and starts on any key.\n6. **HUD icons dim instead of switching style.** Uncollected letters are drawn at `globalAlpha .35` rather than as outlines.\n7. **The 4-tile gap is never tested.** The map contains no 4-tile gap.\n8. **Jump release can be missed.** Releasing the key while a jump is still buffered does not shorten the jump that follows.\n\n**Unverified**\n- Actual jump arcs and landings in a running build.\n- Spike fairness at the 45–50 block, where the fox lands right next to the spikes.\n- Camera feel when the fox turns, since facing shifts the camera target by 96 px.\n- Integer scaling and pixel sharpness.\n- Audio and music.\n- Frame pacing.\n- Overall visual quality against the art plan. No art plan was supplied. The source does draw a sky gradient, sun, towered silhouettes, cumulus clouds, lanterns, potted flowers and vines. However, most terrain runs down to the bottom of the screen, so it reads as pillars rather than floating islands."
